{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact head 8f490e1384a8130117fe0d19ba577f09e03fffdf for request #24568. Examined both changed paths, go.mod and go.sum, with go.mod as the reporting artifact.\n\nArchitecture: the Go toolchain spans the build; CBOR is used by layer 2 Kernel (internal/intent and internal/kernel) and layer 3 live runtime. SQLite is confined to spike/querysandbox, an experimental application-query boundary outside the resident and kernel. The head changes dependencies only and preserves the documented signing, canonical encoding, authority, storage and application-layer contracts. No architecture contract changes or architecture-page amendment are needed.\n\nSecurity: Go remains on the 1.26 line at 1.26.8; CBOR moves to v2.9.4 and SQLite to v0.35.6. go mod verify confirms all module checksums. Upstream SQLite v0.35.6 requires go-sqlite3-wasm/v6 v6.3.35304 and x/sys v0.48.0, and its module also requires x/text v0.42.0; those extra graph changes are necessary dependencies, not unrelated upgrades. The v0.35.5 release notes describe the allocator change and v0.35.6 further performance improvements: https://github.com/ncruces/go-sqlite3/releases/tag/v0.35.5 and https://github.com/ncruces/go-sqlite3/releases/tag/v0.35.6. CBOR v2.9.4 addresses a map-key decoding panic: https://github.com/fxamacker/cbor/releases/tag/v2.9.4. Gitseq retains its bounded, tag-forbidding decoder and fixed-array intent format. Read-only SQL, authorizer, cancellation and result bounds remain unchanged. The full passing race gate includes existing signing/encoding tests and query-sandbox authorizer and cancellation mutation proofs. govulncheck@v1.1.4 reports no vulnerabilities on the declared Go 1.26.8 toolchain.\n\nSimplification: only go.mod and go.sum change. The required SQLite dependency closure accounts for the apparent extra module updates, including the WASM major-path move. No source migration, unrelated update or new guard was added. Existing guards are exercised by their established tests and mutation proofs.\n\nIndependent checks in a clean detached checkout at the exact head, using GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.26.8: go version confirms go1.26.8 darwin/arm64; go mod verify, make vet, make build, govulncheck@v1.1.4 and the final full make race all exit 0. Documentation, canonical intent, kernel, host, persistence, and query-sandbox packages pass.\n\nVerification history: the initial full make race failed only TestAnIncompleteAssociationWithholdsTheCleanupAdviceToo/per-tip_depth_limit: it still withheld cleanup advice but reported commit lineage unavailable rather than the per-tip bound. The source is unchanged from parent e2c02d62d084e838e6a4630d2eaef2a3ae8e8859 and gives the shared Git read a three-second deadline. A deadline under load is a plausible explanation, not a proven cause. The exact subtest passed three isolated candidate runs and one parent run on Go 1.26.7; then the full make race rerun passed, including internal/app. The initial failure is retained rather than counted as a passing gate.\n\nLogs: /tmp/codex-go-release-race.log (initial failure), /tmp/codex-go-release-failed-case.log, /tmp/codex-go-release-parent-case.log, /tmp/codex-go-release-race-rerun.log (passing full gate), and /tmp/codex-go-release-{version,verify,vet,build,vuln}.log. Review includes Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions; no unresolved defect in this dependency head was found. Final Linux CI and Security on the landed release head remain the separate request #24569.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:f81bb33f8e86dbf96faaeff969cbeb9c07c35902","binding":"assigned","head":"8f490e1384a8130117fe0d19ba577f09e03fffdf","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03a7f0e2ef8569ba29cc06a248f38a8fdb54fa70\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:cfe870f429c650fd39e96894fa700e0282ef9a19\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0ce4764e33a01404781af6f4b268d64b8aacaf4b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}